  "question": {
    "text": "An open manometer attached to a flask containing ammonia gas have no difference in mercury level initially as shown in diagram. After sparking into the flask, ammonia is partially dissociated as <math> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <msub> <mtext>NH</mtext> <mn>3</mn> </msub> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>g</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> <mo>⟶</mo> <msub> <mtext>N</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>g</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> <mo>+</mo> <mn>3</mn> <msub> <mtext>H</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mtext>g</mtext> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> </math>. Now it have difference of <math> <mrow> <mtext>18</mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext>cm</mtext></mrow> </math> in mercury level in two columns, what is partial pressure of <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>H</mtext> <mtext>2</mtext> </msub> <mfenced> <mtext>g</mtext> </mfenced></mrow> </math> at equilibrium ?<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0021971_Quest_1_1.jpg\" style=\"width: 253px; height: 150px;\" />",
